{"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Performance","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The binary-size budget","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","level":2,"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Renders the right content for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":", switching between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"title":"ScreenStateView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refresh(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreC5Valuexmfp","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but keeps any data already in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" on screen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"type":"text","text":" runs instead of switching to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern behind pull-to-refresh, where the list shouldn’t disappear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while it’s being refetched. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duration. On success "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is replaced as usual; on failure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is left alone and the error is reported via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/refresh(_:)","title":"refresh(_:)"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/isRefreshing":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isRefreshing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" while "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is fetching"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the background with the previous data still shown in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/isrefreshing","title":"isRefreshing"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/loadCollection(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadCollection(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but maps an empty result to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — convenient when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Value"},{"type":"text","text":" is a list of items to display."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"loadCollection","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreCAASlRzlE5Valuexmfp","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/loadcollection(_:)","title":"loadCollection(_:)"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" holder of a screen’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":", driving both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth."}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateS